Z||000009||Cliff Pennock||12-30-2001||05:17 AM||||I appreciate the gesture, I really do. There are several reasons I don't accept money for the forum. First of all, I see the forum as one of my hobbies. Hobbies cost money - always. And I do use the server for a few other things, mainly hosting websites for a few clients.<P>Second, and this is a slightly delicate subject, but <B>not</B> asking money for it gives me a certain amount of freedom. The only reason I can enforce certain "rules" on this forum is because it's free. Some people seem to think that paying money automatically means they can derive certain rights from it.<P>Let me give an example. Some time ago, I had sent a Private Message to someone asking not to do something (I'm deliberatly being vague here) because it was in violation with a certain rule on this forum. The response I got was that it was a stupid rule and that he saw no reason to honor my request. I then told him this is a free service and that the only thing I ask in return is to follow the few rules I've set. His response was that people had offered me to pay for this and that <B>I</B> have been the one declining it, so I should "shut up" (his exact words). This was a long time member of the forum and just because <B>other</B> people had offered me money for this, he believed he had a right to do what he did. He eventually did what I asked him to do, but under protest. In fact, he gave me a hard time about it for some time after.<P>The problem is that some people are unable to distinguish between a donation and "buying forum time". To avoid such problems, I don't accept any donations for usage of the forum.<P>I'll be honest with you. Of course I would love to find a way to make some extra money through the forum. But it'll have to be something else than paying for usage. I'm open to ideas.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||fierospeeder||12-30-2001||07:08 AM||||cliff, how about opening a thread and having 30 pop up windows to appear?<P><BR>you can setup a members club, and we just pay for electronic email of interesting fiero info.<P>selling pff cds on ebay||||reg||1
Z||000011||hugh||12-30-2001||08:07 AM||||Cliff,In New Jersey,where I live when you get a drivers license it is understood that it is a privilage,not a right.It is probably the same everywhere.When I buy a subscription to a magazine,I only buy the magazine,not the right to tell the editors or managers what they can and cannot do with it.<BR>   What I am getting at is being on this forum is a privilage not a right.If the privilage is abused,then that abuser should suffer the consequences.Paying a subscription to this forum doesn't give anyone who is a member the right to tell you how to run it.Almost all members know this,and I am sure agree with it.You concern yourself too much with the few boneheads who wouldn't know a good thing if it bit them on the ass.We are better off without them.You can charge a subscription fee that is refundable if you have to boot someone and it makes you feel uncomfortable.<BR>  I must be crazy to campaign so hard to spend money for something that is now free.<BR> I just want to pay my way! ||||reg||14
Z||000012||Jaygee79||12-30-2001||09:25 AM||||I would prefer to pay Cliff also, but I do understand his reasons for not accepting it.<P>I don't know how hard this would be, but could you set something up so that if one particular member is giving trouble they wouldn't be able to post without authorization?  Their posts would have to be read and authorized before actually posted to the forum.  I know that would be a lot of reading for one person, so maybe 1 or 2 moderators?  i know that's been discussed before but I'm not sure exactly what the decision was or if there even waqs one.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Jaime<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79   ICQ: 85931334</FONT><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jaygee79sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
