Z||000014||Patrick's Dad||12-30-2001||04:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>When I buy a subscription to a magazine,I only buy the magazine,not the right to tell the editors or managers what they can and cannot do with it.</B> <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, writing the editors often ellicits a change. They are in business to serve their readership, and if your suggestion merits consideration, then its implementation may get more readers, and, therefore, more paycheck.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR> <B>What I am getting at is being on this forum is a privilage not a right. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This is true, but the proper analogy is that we are guests in Cliff's house. He cleans up after us and kicks out the unruly, and he has done so for a few years now. We appreciate this greatly, and until he decides to charge us admission, we should be as gracious as possible to him and to each other.<P>Cliff, how about a referal program? *I'm sure* that many of the vendors wouldn't mind a little kickback.... OTOH, Amazon, B&N, and many other sites have referral programs. Maybe as "payment,' someone would be willing to research these, find stuff that we Fieroites would enjoy (books, tools, etc.) and work with you to set up affiliations. As each of us buy stuff via links from the Forum, you cash in, at least a little bit.||||reg||1
